  "intro": {
    "en": "In week 1 you met the Blackbird, and the Blackbird is a thrush. So are the four birds in this lesson: two that live here all year, and two that come from Scandinavia for the winter. They are all brown or grey above, with spotted breasts.\n\nThat's where it gets tricky: they look alike at first. But once you know what to look at, the spots, the colour of the underwing and the stripe above the eye, you can tell them apart in seconds.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of eight questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
  "words": [
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "underwing"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The underside of the wing. You mostly see it in flight."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "tail corners"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The corners at the end of the tail, on the left and right."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "armpit"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The place under the wing, where it joins the body."
      }
    }
  ],
